### S02
EFFORT: light
ASKED: yes
Two of your requirements pull against each other, so I need to check what you meant before writing the prompt.

**1 - "Works fully offline" against "every save must require an internet connection to sync."**
Offline means the app keeps working with no connection at all; requiring a connection before you can save undoes that. I'd suggest offline-first: you can create and edit notes with no connection, and they sync by themselves once you're back online.

**2 - "Looks professional" against "don't use CSS at all."**
In a browser, all the visual styling is normally done with CSS. With none at all, the page falls back to the browser's plain default look, which won't come across as professional.
- Use a ready-made interface library that brings its own styling. I'd suggest this.
- Keep absolutely no CSS of any kind and accept a plain, unstyled page.
Not sure? Tell me which trade-off matters more and I'll go with it.

